#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059392 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3332b534-bd04-5e86-995e-1e6d691d8e1b" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring and Using the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "762e323d-62be-5cd0-ad06-7b11af56fe3f" :question/math-academy-id "e-3136" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\sin^4{\\theta}+\\sin^2{\\theta}\\cos^2{\\theta}$." :question/worked-solution "First, we factor $\\sin^2\\theta$ from the expression:\n\n$$\n\\sin^4{\\theta}+\\sin^2{\\theta}\\cos^2{\\theta} = \\sin^2{\\theta}\\cdot(\\sin^2{\\theta}+\\cos^2{\\theta})\n$$\n\nThen, we use\n\n$$\n\\cos^2\\theta + \\sin^2\\theta = 1\n$$\n\nto simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin^{2} \\theta  \\cdot (\\sin^{2} \\theta  + \\cos^{2}) &= \\sin^{2} \\theta  \\cdot 1 = \\sin^{2} \\theta \n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\sin^4{\\theta}+\\sin^2{\\theta}\\cos^2{\\theta} = \\sin^2\\theta\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059393 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "868125f0-22e0-57fc-9620-f3242419a689" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Rational Expression Using the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "f2b7e482-2bcd-5bd2-91ee-66415b375da4" :question/math-academy-id "e-3137" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\dfrac {\\cos \\theta \\sin^2 \\theta + \\cos^3 \\theta}{\\sin\\theta}$." :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\cos \\theta \\sin^2 \\theta + \\cos^3 \\theta} {\\sin \\theta} = \\dfrac {\\cos \\theta \\cdot (\\sin^2 \\theta + \\cos^2 \\theta)} {\\sin \\theta}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible.\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\frac{\\cos   \\theta  \\cdot  ( {\\sin }^{2}  \\theta  + {\\cos }^{2}  \\theta  )}{\\sin   \\theta} & = \\frac{\\cos   \\theta  \\cdot  ( 1 )}{\\sin   \\theta} \\\\  & = \\frac{\\cos   \\theta}{\\sin   \\theta} \\\\  & = \\cot   \\theta\\end{array}$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\cos \\theta \\sin^2 \\theta + \\cos^3 \\theta} {\\sin \\theta} = \\cot \\theta\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059394 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1bc8c875-3393-5fd6-90cf-87737e16f2f2" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Trigonometric Expression Using a Common Denominator and the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "9ee1e04e-8a36-5597-8928-c2ebd67c1b1a" :question/math-academy-id "e-3139" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\dfrac{\\sin{\\theta}}{1+\\cos{\\theta}}+\\cot{\\theta}$." :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the second term using the identity\n\n$$\n\\cot \\theta = \\dfrac{\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}\n$$\n\nas follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\sin{\\theta}}{1+\\cos{\\theta}}+\\dfrac{\\cos{\\theta}}{\\sin{\\theta}}\n$$\n\nNext, we put both terms over a common denominator, and combine the two fractions:\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\frac{\\sin   \\theta \\cdot  \\sin   \\theta}{\\sin   \\theta  ( 1 + \\cos   \\theta )} + \\frac{\\cos   \\theta \\cdot  ( 1 + \\cos   \\theta  )}{\\sin   \\theta ( 1 + \\cos   \\theta )} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sin   \\theta \\cdot  \\sin   \\theta + \\cos   \\theta \\cdot  ( 1 + \\cos   \\theta )}{\\sin   \\theta ( 1 + \\cos   \\theta )} & \\end{array}$$\n\nFinally, we simplify as follows:\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\frac{{\\sin }^{2}  \\theta + \\cos   \\theta + {\\cos }^{2}  \\theta}{\\sin   \\theta ( 1 + \\cos   \\theta )} & = \\\\ \\frac{( {\\sin }^{2}  \\theta + {\\cos }^{2}  \\theta ) + \\cos   \\theta}{\\sin   \\theta ( 1 + \\cos   \\theta )} & = \\\\ \\frac{1 + \\cos   \\theta}{\\sin   \\theta ( 1 + \\cos   \\theta )} & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sin   \\theta} & = \\\\ \\csc   \\theta\\end{array}$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\sin{\\theta}}{1+\\cos{\\theta}}+\\cot{\\theta} = \\csc\\theta\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059409 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec62fd08-5729-5dc4-97b9-1a422f70109e" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Expanding Parentheses and Using the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "d917e025-59a4-5df5-b412-4eb6f2c4afc7" :question/math-academy-id "e-3329" :question/problem "Simplify the expression $\\sin x(2\\cos x - \\sin x) - \\cos^2x$." :question/worked-solution "First, we expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n2\\sin x\\cos x - \\sin^{2} x - \\cos^{2} x\n$$\n\nNext, we group the $\\sin^2 x$ and $\\cos^2 x$ terms.\n\n$$\n2\\sin x\\cos x -(\\sin^2x + \\cos^2 x)\n$$\n\nThen, we use\n\n$$\n\\sin^2{x} + \\cos^2{x} = 1\n$$\n\nto simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n2\\sin x\\cos x - 1\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\sin x(2\\cos x - \\sin x) - \\cos^2x = 2\\sin x\\cos x - 1\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255646 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec62fd08-5729-5dc4-97b9-1a422f70109e" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Expanding Parentheses and Using the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f67130f-2b20-5f84-b4c1-e94e924abd3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255648} {:answer/id #uuid "44237afa-c80b-55d7-ac41-2b72b86ffc1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255649} {:answer/id #uuid "fed70dca-17cb-5fac-b9f9-e3c38b3f702d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255650} {:answer/id #uuid "dc3a216b-d8e4-505f-8346-56f60d0a21ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255651} {:answer/id #uuid "b68db269-d285-5013-a1a9-4aeefdd09462" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255652}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fed70dca-17cb-5fac-b9f9-e3c38b3f702d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255650} :answer-field/id #uuid "66bc5e35-96d1-5349-a6bb-a7143fe23a5a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255647}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c4c8e89c-b26a-532f-8913-ca99a283c33a" :question/math-academy-id "q-119361" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta (\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta })+{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =$" :question/worked-solution "First, we expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta (\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta })+{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }+{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }}+{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +1+{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =1+({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ) \\\\  & =1+1 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that, in the last step, we simplified the right-hand side using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.$ \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta (\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta })+{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255653 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3332b534-bd04-5e86-995e-1e6d691d8e1b" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring and Using the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6bc6834c-6522-5d30-a831-c2b356b91403" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255655} {:answer/id #uuid "20452ace-e4f8-5717-917d-19d12f9a4a08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255656} {:answer/id #uuid "106b8ed0-ad83-54d5-9101-a32f2631ea05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255657} {:answer/id #uuid "7ee0dd13-ebc9-57cc-a016-c716e42eb7e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255658} {:answer/id #uuid "896537f5-247e-5f7a-b568-9c2ed74f1036" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255659}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6bc6834c-6522-5d30-a831-c2b356b91403" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255655} :answer-field/id #uuid "aaed3e75-c408-5078-b2d1-bb2dd5c4decd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255654}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "402fcfb6-7d80-5234-a3b7-1b8c7a836281" :question/math-academy-id "q-119367" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the expression:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\n$$\n\nThen, we use ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255660 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3332b534-bd04-5e86-995e-1e6d691d8e1b" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring and Using the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85fa7a30-8470-5d67-924b-5cb149febfd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255662} {:answer/id #uuid "e91d17ac-40d2-5dba-a35f-73009ee920ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255663} {:answer/id #uuid "3e0c90c8-6aa0-5b10-ba66-e7ad1ee52811" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255664} {:answer/id #uuid "36379d93-653f-52f1-ae5f-de903f4341b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255665} {:answer/id #uuid "3f0beb6d-c093-5d35-96c3-0aeca2b47823" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255666}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f0beb6d-c093-5d35-96c3-0aeca2b47823" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255666} :answer-field/id #uuid "96f0f3c8-986c-5210-9d75-13abbf8a8a94" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255661}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5b78db70-978b-55b5-81c7-ce8fa0763cd8" :question/math-academy-id "q-119371" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression ${sin}^{3}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the expression:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nThen, we use ${sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot 1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255667 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "868125f0-22e0-57fc-9620-f3242419a689" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Rational Expression Using the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "778237c3-895e-55bb-b150-48f1c8f5d6cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255669} {:answer/id #uuid "e518a321-2f53-5c86-bd6b-5d3ca27b3199" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255670} {:answer/id #uuid "ac72b2cf-d7be-5f2c-8fb0-3e63de067e6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255671} {:answer/id #uuid "017a304a-5599-5c27-85d2-a1b49917bfb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255672} {:answer/id #uuid "09a5b962-7cff-582b-bc2f-8a4c46e3af2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255673}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09a5b962-7cff-582b-bc2f-8a4c46e3af2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255673} :answer-field/id #uuid "77361238-17d3-5cd7-8510-3767db94a1b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255668}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "61188e95-01a2-5109-b80e-5a0ee0202f78" :question/math-academy-id "q-119379" :question/problem "$\\frac{{sin}^{3}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{4}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sin}^{3}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{4}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x\\cdot 1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{1} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sin}^{3}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{4}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255674 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1bc8c875-3393-5fd6-90cf-87737e16f2f2" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Trigonometric Expression Using a Common Denominator and the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e2e0c4f-3f6f-598d-ad82-a2d0810ce0a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255676} {:answer/id #uuid "80fab331-80c5-5498-b2c2-f14d08a434c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255677} {:answer/id #uuid "6c5d4bb1-8b42-5105-9758-25703be29a9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255678} {:answer/id #uuid "79dd7b94-72b2-58cc-ada3-9fd34c66564c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255679} {:answer/id #uuid "11c5a9ff-2ae0-54b7-addd-8a6afdb1631f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255680}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e2e0c4f-3f6f-598d-ad82-a2d0810ce0a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255676} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5bcad66-2a74-5df9-9f28-2f374449287b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255675}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "16e67eb5-9ab5-5db6-972a-fe73b4e9d7ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-119764" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the first term using the definition of $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nNow, we put both terms over a common denominator, and combine the two fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}-\\frac{(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-{cos}^{2}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify using the Pythagorean identity, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =\\frac{({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255681 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1bc8c875-3393-5fd6-90cf-87737e16f2f2" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Trigonometric Expression Using a Common Denominator and the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3608fce5-7a36-59cc-a03e-8b319fb750ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255683} {:answer/id #uuid "1968475b-8db5-51d2-ae0e-0c05a65b12c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255684} {:answer/id #uuid "b057a6ec-8c6e-5e24-9422-bb2017715602" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255685} {:answer/id #uuid "3baeed5d-a91e-553c-b2a5-210d36c4da33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255686} {:answer/id #uuid "07370b15-579e-54a7-9139-cca64bc6cdd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255687}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b057a6ec-8c6e-5e24-9422-bb2017715602" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255685} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1a74c6d-2940-57e2-93fc-fbc471b9da48" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255682}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "18cf754a-f949-5f84-80b0-3481b58e5682" :question/math-academy-id "q-119770" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "We put both terms over a common denominator, and combine the two fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{1(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify using the Pythagorean identity, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255688 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec62fd08-5729-5dc4-97b9-1a422f70109e" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Expanding Parentheses and Using the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18cbc9e0-efb2-55ee-a6e5-b7bdc5d0c084" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255690} {:answer/id #uuid "a208c787-c952-5c5a-b572-de3af055869a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255691} {:answer/id #uuid "995f7257-8117-558f-a701-8bca520d2dd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255692} {:answer/id #uuid "ff092e9a-2faa-58d2-8b89-f5a29ef55324" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255693} {:answer/id #uuid "ab86bdf4-4c22-5211-bb6a-7c5d6c31352a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255694}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a208c787-c952-5c5a-b572-de3af055869a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255691} :answer-field/id #uuid "66a1fea4-d4af-59b3-bf6a-da11181e6c54" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255689}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "da274cb8-890f-5614-be3f-338930f5247d" :question/math-academy-id "q-43288" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta (\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta })=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta (\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }+\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }}+\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }} \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that, in the last step, we simplified the right-hand side using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.$ \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta (\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta })=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255695 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec62fd08-5729-5dc4-97b9-1a422f70109e" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Expanding Parentheses and Using the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f720f87e-ee42-5d38-8375-28d6f4a924f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255697} {:answer/id #uuid "b8258e08-92ea-5bf7-8f52-ce35a4ad4d74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255698} {:answer/id #uuid "18e03c99-48ac-5918-9066-8d03a5b2b0bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255699} {:answer/id #uuid "545aa608-c44d-569c-8fc8-7d60506d36c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255700} {:answer/id #uuid "df25dc03-3399-5bc6-aa2f-54be96541b37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255701}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8258e08-92ea-5bf7-8f52-ce35a4ad4d74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255698} :answer-field/id #uuid "34494ea4-e524-5585-b66a-7be2ecc3f8c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255696}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cb49b0b4-be72-55e6-95b9-ba62b8d9d278" :question/math-academy-id "q-43293" :question/problem "$\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }({sin}^{3}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }({sin}^{3}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ) & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\cdot {sin}^{3}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }+\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }}+\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }} \\\\  & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that, in the last step, we simplified the right-hand side using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.$ \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }({sin}^{3}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255702 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1bc8c875-3393-5fd6-90cf-87737e16f2f2" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Trigonometric Expression Using a Common Denominator and the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f9d03c6b-ffa9-5e09-bf6e-1d1974df4eac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255704} {:answer/id #uuid "ac096f3b-4116-551c-99fb-ead3b28b60bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡t+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255705} {:answer/id #uuid "9a5c6a24-e8ec-5ce2-a02e-15841cfada8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sec}⁡t-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255706} {:answer/id #uuid "bdb81bf9-aea3-5bc7-91ff-90f9b8effe06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sec}⁡t+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255707} {:answer/id #uuid "86691e56-de82-5341-a222-d83bcd938a2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255708}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9d03c6b-ffa9-5e09-bf6e-1d1974df4eac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255704} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c64d797-0ea1-5452-90e3-ae2360aeb0a5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255703}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "653aef88-f856-52e1-a486-3e093039ce1a" :question/math-academy-id "q-43298" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{sin}⁡t(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t})=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}+\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot \\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}}+\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe put both terms over a common denominator, and combine the two fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{1}+\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{1\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t}+\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify using the Pythagorean identity, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡t(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t})=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255709 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec62fd08-5729-5dc4-97b9-1a422f70109e" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Expanding Parentheses and Using the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44e581b8-8048-5bc7-8a56-245755d886cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255711} {:answer/id #uuid "104d1683-cef5-5b73-9cbe-7ab946b00322" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255712} {:answer/id #uuid "4ecd62f0-49bc-5e45-97a8-03eb2f64a727" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255713} {:answer/id #uuid "845a29ad-7cbf-5c9b-96e8-b9af821f49e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255714} {:answer/id #uuid "5a1471e9-dbe1-5ad1-a1ce-8cb57d144fc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255715}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a1471e9-dbe1-5ad1-a1ce-8cb57d144fc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255715} :answer-field/id #uuid "913666bc-6e16-5a47-bfc0-f08a87654960" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255710}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2cd9b6ea-7f4c-565f-a1df-e0c0764d8805" :question/math-academy-id "q-65222" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\operatorname{cos}⁡t(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)-{sin}^{2}⁡t.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)-{sin}^{2}⁡t & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that, in the last step, we simplified the right-hand side using ${cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t=1.$ \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡t(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)-{sin}^{2}⁡t=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255716 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec62fd08-5729-5dc4-97b9-1a422f70109e" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Expanding Parentheses and Using the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96a2534a-4eeb-5f0c-9818-5e4f12646849" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255718} {:answer/id #uuid "c309d3c7-c157-5466-a966-6243e92f1998" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255719} {:answer/id #uuid "a7047058-1e1a-5d88-895c-e78fd8734d36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255720} {:answer/id #uuid "b295ce26-d4ba-51d3-a4d5-c9e92c2ce646" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255721} {:answer/id #uuid "debf1862-f425-5935-9149-b6ae0226abac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255722}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c309d3c7-c157-5466-a966-6243e92f1998" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255719} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4524c72-f15b-5742-92da-4422245d8dd1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255717}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "16d44cc7-1923-56da-8842-da86595c2fb9" :question/math-academy-id "q-65225" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{sin}⁡t(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-1)+{cos}^{2}⁡t=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-1)+{cos}^{2}⁡t & ={sin}^{2}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\  & =1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that, in the last step, we simplified the right-hand side using ${cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t=1.$ \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡t(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-1)+{cos}^{2}⁡t=1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255723 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3332b534-bd04-5e86-995e-1e6d691d8e1b" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring and Using the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f0c74c88-d5c4-5fbe-a92e-db606974d622" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255725} {:answer/id #uuid "bef5bc42-7e55-56f9-bc96-affac3712522" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255726} {:answer/id #uuid "9122bd3c-ac58-5718-8292-7ef28f64d767" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255727} {:answer/id #uuid "c8c7bcaf-a4d2-540c-be1e-404cb52538a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255728} {:answer/id #uuid "32b74013-db6e-5fbb-968a-0f5c5555838e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255729}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9122bd3c-ac58-5718-8292-7ef28f64d767" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255727} :answer-field/id #uuid "24b03677-9d62-56e1-94e4-d3396ffaac8e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255724}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c6e920ec-c082-580c-82aa-33c74278971d" :question/math-academy-id "q-65241" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{3}⁡x+{sin}^{3}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ from the expression:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{3}⁡x+{sin}^{3}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot ({cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x)\n$$\n\nThen, we use ${cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot ({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{3}⁡x+{sin}^{3}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255730 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3332b534-bd04-5e86-995e-1e6d691d8e1b" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring and Using the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b14398f0-fa09-5b84-b3eb-d103893ca3e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255732} {:answer/id #uuid "81b34acd-ec55-5c9a-8757-4df4878bafed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255733} {:answer/id #uuid "c6e137ea-be1e-587a-823a-37f45e1c9e3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255734} {:answer/id #uuid "2caccb9c-c839-5d81-9e3f-d53d8b00c65e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255735} {:answer/id #uuid "033d7da4-4ae0-5da0-bfa6-2bdc8f9135ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255736}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81b34acd-ec55-5c9a-8757-4df4878bafed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255733} :answer-field/id #uuid "cea806df-eed4-55c6-9699-9ae2e1c365aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255731}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b6342f91-f989-57b2-95ed-f8a24b7aafd9" :question/math-academy-id "q-65243" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression ${sin}^{2}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{4}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor ${cos}^{2}⁡x$  from the first two terms:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{4}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x={cos}^{2}⁡x\\cdot ({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)+{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nThen, we use ${cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1$ to simplify the given expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡x\\cdot ({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)+{sin}^{2}⁡x & ={cos}^{2}⁡x\\cdot 1+{sin}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{4}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255737 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "868125f0-22e0-57fc-9620-f3242419a689" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Rational Expression Using the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27ba11c6-3fa7-57ac-b319-ebc3c49c3b05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255739} {:answer/id #uuid "d5819a82-cc98-545d-a483-23070e5eae1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255740} {:answer/id #uuid "b6bcb8b1-e862-583d-b8bd-adffd45d0a24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡t+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255741} {:answer/id #uuid "834f44dd-de8f-5eb7-9aaa-33d6c6c28f8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255742} {:answer/id #uuid "0fe1721e-f082-5f06-95cc-143c61c2fa4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡t-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255743}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27ba11c6-3fa7-57ac-b319-ebc3c49c3b05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255739} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9be4375-ef89-5adf-82a7-62f9713e002b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255738}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8061b56b-2d07-50c1-8c04-c9abe9212787" :question/math-academy-id "q-65246" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{3}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{3}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot ({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot ({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot 1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{3}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255744 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "868125f0-22e0-57fc-9620-f3242419a689" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Rational Expression Using the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f02f473-9f74-5589-8eb6-5719be61a940" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255746} {:answer/id #uuid "a5faf8a6-1e60-5284-b285-cd4d887becc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255747} {:answer/id #uuid "c9f67bce-62a0-56c2-8778-209f3a6836a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255748} {:answer/id #uuid "8bad9c67-a453-58bf-b8f0-88a29fd9843e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255749} {:answer/id #uuid "02d0d7a6-df9e-5a36-8a57-315f9079fae3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255750}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5faf8a6-1e60-5284-b285-cd4d887becc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255747} :answer-field/id #uuid "884430ea-5ba5-55e1-8ae4-d89e76c33296" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255745}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cca918fe-5255-5aea-b94f-756cef87e865" :question/math-academy-id "q-65248" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{3}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{3}⁡\\theta }.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{3}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{3}⁡\\theta }=\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot ({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot ({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )} & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{3}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{3}⁡\\theta }=\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255751 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "868125f0-22e0-57fc-9620-f3242419a689" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Rational Expression Using the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f85a2ef9-e633-58fd-9a74-01bb6cdd3e73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255753} {:answer/id #uuid "99f12ab1-43f0-545e-9116-e7f3d5139227" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255754} {:answer/id #uuid "d68b9176-487c-54ac-9e92-1343b6c283ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255755} {:answer/id #uuid "8ec639bd-874d-512e-8914-ae3d5b7bab68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255756} {:answer/id #uuid "74a10c15-ba27-58d9-b6fa-363a55b245dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255757}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74a10c15-ba27-58d9-b6fa-363a55b245dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255757} :answer-field/id #uuid "7eb84438-f9e6-51c7-9620-0e276c988975" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255752}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ee45ffe7-242c-52a4-ae69-0bd185f65858" :question/math-academy-id "q-65249" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{4}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{4}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot ({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot ({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{4}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }=\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255758 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1bc8c875-3393-5fd6-90cf-87737e16f2f2" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Trigonometric Expression Using a Common Denominator and the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48a3eccf-a2b6-59b8-b9eb-8e4bf5301b49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255760} {:answer/id #uuid "4dfd2733-3e5f-5571-825c-48b266e9beb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255761} {:answer/id #uuid "e478993f-1811-5166-b1f2-9b1ddc0ffe13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255762} {:answer/id #uuid "3c1a775b-d564-5678-92ce-9413c57a6f6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255763} {:answer/id #uuid "722fb7af-7218-5327-9ca4-6b8aaf2e7c46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255764}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e478993f-1811-5166-b1f2-9b1ddc0ffe13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255762} :answer-field/id #uuid "5007e5c4-a4a7-58a5-a51a-3a7b7de8e52e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255759}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "014608d1-fbaf-5fcc-9043-6ed08ac54812" :question/math-academy-id "q-65254" :question/problem "$\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=$" :question/worked-solution "We put both terms over a common denominator, and combine the two fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{1} \\\\  & \\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}{1(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{({cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255765 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3332b534-bd04-5e86-995e-1e6d691d8e1b" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring and Using the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ead98285-9b82-58d6-9a3a-a486f8beedd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255767} {:answer/id #uuid "d5156149-d27c-5e0b-9cdc-404e744e22fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255768} {:answer/id #uuid "aa4fea81-d457-5d8d-9bd7-9dabfcdbdc07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255769} {:answer/id #uuid "cd57a8b1-e5aa-5580-84f3-1eed37a59f53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255770} {:answer/id #uuid "3620c990-9edf-50ca-beec-6e368b36a7f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255771}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ead98285-9b82-58d6-9a3a-a486f8beedd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255767} :answer-field/id #uuid "077f1aab-c195-52f9-9442-3a58daedabd9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255766}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "717ddb1a-fa2a-5d1c-9bf1-d894fce007ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-72711" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2{cos}^{3}⁡x+2{sin}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the expression:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2{cos}^{3}⁡x+2{sin}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x({cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x)\n$$\n\nThen, we use ${cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x({cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2{cos}^{3}⁡x+2{sin}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255772 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "868125f0-22e0-57fc-9620-f3242419a689" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Rational Expression Using the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "652a519e-6044-55c9-b687-0eaf451aa4e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255774} {:answer/id #uuid "fe24a001-2ae3-5a28-96d0-c946472cf018" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255775} {:answer/id #uuid "4d3a48f8-a132-58be-9a77-da5d9e88636a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255776} {:answer/id #uuid "4c790421-55f1-5db7-ab84-46756901b08d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255777} {:answer/id #uuid "b183d013-5c59-545c-b71e-05d9cedefb80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255778}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b183d013-5c59-545c-b71e-05d9cedefb80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255778} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebca33b5-a1ca-561d-a53a-a7f4a65957ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255773}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2f4cf1a9-f966-55f5-ad06-7ce4a1647800" :question/math-academy-id "q-72712" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\frac{{sin}^{3}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ from the first two terms:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sin}^{3}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)+1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)+1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sin}^{3}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255779 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1bc8c875-3393-5fd6-90cf-87737e16f2f2" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Trigonometric Expression Using a Common Denominator and the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2724473-e724-50db-a638-d8de10a1e471" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255781} {:answer/id #uuid "f8eb1ad0-d6f6-5e7c-ae54-8a2f5e985ae0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255782} {:answer/id #uuid "cfedd0b7-55e5-5a90-95f0-473d9224b56b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255783} {:answer/id #uuid "9d79977e-ea42-527c-9a76-287b7c71e1e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255784} {:answer/id #uuid "1f15bf8c-1a8b-59a8-b25f-33330d9dcc59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255785}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8eb1ad0-d6f6-5e7c-ae54-8a2f5e985ae0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255782} :answer-field/id #uuid "a500c715-0776-5236-aa09-d237e03c000f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255780}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b5e04a73-9223-5f7f-8ad0-01a1759b4633" :question/math-academy-id "q-72715" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the second term using the definition of $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$ This gives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\n$$\n\nWe put both terms over a common denominator, and combine the two fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =\\frac{(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+({cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\n$$"}]}
